## 5. MVP Scope

The MVP is organised around three core capabilities.

### 5.1 Natural Capture

Parents can create records using:

- Voice input — primary experience.
- Text input — alternative experience.

Examples:

- "Thomas had 90 ml of formula at 2 AM."
- "He slept from 10 until half past eleven."
- "We changed his nappy and it was wet."
- "He breastfed on the left side for around 15 minutes."

The system should support natural language rather than requiring parents to navigate multiple fields.

### 5.2 Automatic Organisation

NapNook uses AI to transform captured information into structured events.

The system should identify, when available:

- Event category.
- Event date and time.
- Duration.
- Quantity.
- Unit of measurement.
- Relevant attributes.
- Additional notes.

The original input should remain associated with the structured record so that parents can understand how it was interpreted.

### 5.3 Shared Memory and Retrieval

Both parents can access the same timeline from their own devices.

They can:

- Browse records chronologically.
- Filter by event category.
- Search historical records.
- View event details.
- Edit or delete records.
- See which records were created or updated by each parent.

