## 9. UX Principles

NapNook should follow these product principles:

### 9.1 Capture in Seconds

Recording an event should require as little interaction as possible.

### 9.2 Voice First, Not Voice Only

Voice is the default capture experience, but text must remain available.

### 9.3 No Pressure to Track Everything

NapNook should support incomplete histories and occasional use.

### 9.4 Shared by Default

Both parents should have the same view of the household history.

### 9.5 AI Should Reduce Work

Parents should not have to understand AI prompts, schemas or structured fields.

### 9.6 Clarity Over Complexity

The interface should prioritise capture, timeline and retrieval rather than dashboards and advanced analytics.

