## 11. Success Metrics

Success should measure reduced effort and reliable information, not simply how frequently parents open the app.

### 11.1 Primary Metrics

| Metric | Initial target | Measurement |
|---|---:|---|
| Median event capture time | Under 15 seconds | Time from capture initiation to confirmed record |
| Event type extraction accuracy | At least 95% | Correct event classifications / evaluated events |
| Provided-field extraction accuracy | At least 90% | Correctly extracted provided fields / evaluated fields |
| Critical invented facts | 0 | Count of unsupported critical values in evaluation |
| Historical retrieval success | At least 90% | Successful retrieval tasks / evaluated tasks |
| Unassisted task completion | At least 80% | Tasks completed without researcher assistance |

These are proposed targets for evaluation, not achieved results or established benchmarks.

### 11.2 Secondary Metrics

- Percentage of AI-generated records corrected before confirmation.
- Percentage of proposed records discarded.
- Voice capture completion rate.
- Synchronisation success rate.
- Time required to retrieve a historical event.
- Parent-reported perceived effort.
- Parent-reported usefulness of the shared timeline.

### 11.3 Guardrail Metrics

- Number of critical unsupported AI claims.
- Number of unauthorised access incidents.
- Number of lost or duplicated records.
- Number of unresolved synchronisation conflicts.
- Number of users reporting that suggestions create pressure.

