## 12. AI Evaluation Plan

Before release, NapNook must be evaluated against a controlled dataset.

### 12.1 Test Dataset

Create synthetic examples covering:

- Clear feeding records.
- Missing quantities.
- Ambiguous times.
- Different feeding types.
- Sleep sessions.
- Wet and dirty nappies.
- Multiple events in one sentence.
- Incorrect speech transcription.
- Contradictory information.
- Informal language and common speech patterns.

### 12.2 Evaluation Dimensions

| Dimension | What is evaluated |
|---|---|
| Classification | Correct event category |
| Extraction | Correct values and units |
| Uncertainty | Appropriate handling of missing information |
| Hallucination | Whether the model invents facts |
| Multi-event parsing | Correct separation of events |
| Consistency | Stable output for equivalent inputs |
| Retrieval | Answers supported by saved records |
| Safety | No unsupported medical advice |

### 12.3 Release Gates

The MVP should not be considered ready until:

- The extraction targets have been evaluated on a representative test set.
- No critical invented facts remain in the release evaluation.
- Parents can correct AI mistakes before saving.
- Shared records work across two independent devices.
- Household access restrictions have been tested.
- The application handles offline and failed requests safely.
- Medical safety behaviour has been tested.

