## 13. Technical Direction — To Be Validated

The following is a proposed implementation direction, not a final architecture commitment.

| Area | Initial direction |
|---|---|
| Mobile application | React Native + Expo + TypeScript |
| Local persistence | SQLite |
| Shared synchronisation | Secure backend and database |
| AI processing | OpenAI API through a secure backend gateway |
| Speech processing | Speech-to-text capability |
| Structured extraction | LLM with schema-constrained output |
| Testing | Unit, integration and end-to-end tests |
| Version control | Public GitHub repository |
| CI/CD | GitHub Actions |

### Architectural Considerations

- The iOS application must never contain a publicly accessible AI API key.
- AI processing must be separated from the mobile client through a secure backend.
- Local persistence and remote synchronisation must support intermittent connectivity.
- The system must enforce two-parent household access.
- The architecture must retain the original user input and the resulting structured event where appropriate.
- Audio retention and deletion must be explicitly defined.
- Data synchronisation must be designed before choosing the final backend.

The technical design will be documented separately in an Architecture Decision Record (ADR).

